Limb Damage Redesign
- With the changes to critical hits, it's now possible (and even likely)
with the current limb damage code for players to scrap the limbs of
end-game mobs in a single crit, trivializing combat.
- To allow limb damage to work within the critical hit update, the way it's
calculated and applied has been redesigned.
- Hits on limbs now do 50% of the incoming damage to the victim's main HP
pool, and 50% to the limb. Damage is reduced by high brawn and increased
by low brawn.
- The values in this update will be subject to frequent change in response
to tester feedback over the next while. The goal is to find a good balance
where limb damage can still affect a fight but isn't the primary goal of
end-game combat, and where the extra damage to the main HP pool isn't too
substantial of an increase.
